.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-BUCKET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-bucket - The team's own S3-compatible bucket (owners and admins)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team bucket [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
A team connects its own S3-compatible bucket and its machines copy closed terminal recordings there, so a recording replays when its machine is offline. Paperboat stores the access key encrypted and only signs short-lived links; everything in the bucket is encrypted before it leaves the machine, and the bucket's own security is the team's.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for bucket


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP, \fBpb-team-bucket-get(1)\fP, \fBpb-team-bucket-remove(1)\fP, \fBpb-team-bucket-set(1)\fP
